    "lesson_num": 17,
    "title": "Правила: Little vs A little, Few vs A few – Grammar Shorts",
    "level": "SHORTS",
    "overview": "Little/few без a часто передают значение «мало, почти недостаточно». A little/a few показывают небольшой, но реальный amount/number.",
    "main_rule": "Little + uncountable. A little + uncountable. Few + plural countable. A few + plural countable.",
    "form": "little/a little + uncountable. few/a few + plural countable.",
    "when_why": "Главное отличие — article a меняет оттенок: almost none/insufficient vs some amount/number.",
    "examples": "We have little time. → У нас мало времени, вероятно, недостаточно.\nWe have a little time. → У нас есть немного времени.\nFew people understood the problem. → Мало кто понял проблему.\nA few people understood the problem. → Несколько человек поняли проблему.",
    "special_cases": "Article a changes meaning significantly. Сравни little hope vs a little hope.",
    "common_mistakes": "❌ a little people → ✅ a few people.\n❌ a few time → ✅ a little time.",
    "dont_confuse": "little/a little → uncountable.\nfew/a few → plural countable.\na = small but real amount/number.",
    "quick_summary": "a little/a few = some.\nlittle/few = not much/not many."
  },
